# shir_nodes/field_grab.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# `${s%%D*}` evaluated over the TAIL of `text` starting at byte offset
# `off`: the head field up to the first `delim` at/after `off`, or the
# whole tail when no `delim` follows `off` (bash leaves the value when
# the pattern does not match). Emitted by the `str-chop-cursor` transform
# together with FieldStrip; together they replace the quadratic
# `x=${s%%D*}; s=${s#*D}` front-chop pair with an O(1) cursor.
#
# Proved: docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Field.thy.
#   spec: field_grab_at_strip — `drop off text = grab @ delim @ drop (strip)`,
#         i.e. the grab and the advance are two readings of ONE cursor
#         position, not two independent moves; the next field is the grab at
#         the offset the previous strip reported.
#   With it: field_hit_occ / field_hit_min / field_hit_none (the hit really is
#   the leftmost occurrence, and a miss really is no occurrence anywhere after
#   the cursor), field_grab_is_tail_prefix (the grab invents nothing),
#   field_grab_at_end (no more fields reads ""), field_init_is_zero (the first
#   grab is the head field) and field_grab_empty_delim_is_not_a_cut (an empty
#   delimiter is NOT the empty-literal cut: the arm's non-empty guard is
#   load-bearing).
#   Same read-law caveat: `off <= strlen(text)` is assumed, not proved here.
#
# Backends: C (strchr-at-offset; target-gated offer — other backends
# accept by adding a render arm and their target to the gate).
# Fallback: sh2.fieldGrab(text, off, delim)

node FieldGrab
tag "FieldGrab"
kind expr
field text: expr
field off: expr
field delim: string
spec: TextOps#field_grab_at_strip
